# Project parity rereview remediation — 2026-10-27

- Plan: `plan/2026/10/03-project-parity-rereview.md` with Traditional Chinese companion; Java oracle Apache RocketMQ client 5.5.1.
- Starting revision: `9b006383fd8c81490c673244d69853b3d8ee89eb`.
- Branch: `fix/parity-rereview-2026-10-27`.
- User constraint: the plan may be committed; keep all files under `plan/2026/10/03-project-parity-rereview-evidence/` out of commits. The previous `02-project-parity-review-evidence/` is also preserved and excluded.
- The `coding` skill phased workflow is in use. The plan and this append-only log are eligible for commit; evidence files are not.

## Phase 1 — F01 Lite poll delivery with nullable group

- `LitePullConsumer::poll` now skips consume-hook context construction when no hooks are installed, so a nullable live group cannot fail after the ready batch has been removed.
- When hooks are installed, a null live group is retained as `None` in `ConsumeMessageContext`, matching Java. Group/namespace preparation occurs only for the hook path.
- Extended the external scripted Lite flow to set the group to null after startup, deliver a valid queued message, restore the group, commit the queue, and assert persisted offset 1. Updated the hook unit case to verify a null group reaches both callbacks' shared context path.
- Focused checks passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked --test lite_pop scripted_lite_helpers_cover_assignment_offsets_commits_and_name_server_updates` and `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked lite_poll_consume_hooks_run_around_delivery_with_queue_metadata`.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` will be recorded after final phase checks. Phase 1 commit is the changeset containing this entry.
- Formatting follow-up: the initial format check identified one expected rustfmt layout change in the new hook-context construction; `cargo fmt --all` applied it, and the subsequent format check and `git diff --check` passed.

## Phase 2 — F02 compact inner decoding and F04 public decompression

- Replaced Consumer's duplicate compact-record parser and its 16 MiB per-record / 64 MiB aggregate limits with Common's `decode_inner_batch`; compact decode failures still trigger the existing all-or-original fallback.
- Added `PullAPIWrapper` regressions for 24 × 3 MiB compact messages, one 17 MiB compact message, mixed ordinary/inner records, offsets, tags, unique/client IDs, client subtype, inherited WAIT true/false, and malformed fallback.
- Public `compression::decompress` now delegates to the bounded implementation with the full `usize` output domain. Internal message decode continues to use its explicit bounded helper.
- Added 65 MiB round-trips for Zlib/LZ4/Zstd, malformed input checks for all codecs, and a Producer compressor test proving its public round-trip and returned-type snapshot behavior.
- Focused checks passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked pull_processing_` (4 passed); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --locked public_decompression` (1 passed); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --locked every_public_decompressor` (1 passed); `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked producer_compressor_round_trips_large_body` (1 passed).
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed. Java differential replay will be run after the remaining F03/F05 state changes and its evidence will remain untracked.
- Phase 1 changeset: `92940332` (`Preserve Lite poll batches with nullable groups`).
